{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Topic Modeling \u2014 LDA and BERTopic Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: LDA via scikit-learn"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.feature_extraction.text import CountVectorizer"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from sklearn.decomposition import LatentDirichletAllocation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "import numpy as np"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def fit_lda(documents, n_topics=5, max_features=1000):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    cv = CountVectorizer("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        max_features=max_features,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        stop_words=\"english\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        min_df=2,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        max_df=0.9,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    X = cv.fit_transform(documents)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    lda = LatentDirichletAllocation("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        n_components=n_topics,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        random_state=42,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        max_iter=50,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        learning_method=\"online\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    )"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    doc_topic = lda.fit_transform(X)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    feature_names = cv.get_feature_names_out()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return lda, cv, doc_topic, feature_names"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def print_top_words(lda, feature_names, n_top=10):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for idx, topic in enumerate(lda.components_):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        top_idx = np.argsort(-topic)[:n_top]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        words = [feature_names[i] for i in top_idx]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        print(f\"topic {idx}: {' '.join(words)}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Notice: stopwords removed, min_df and max_df filter rare and ubiquitous terms, CountVectorizer (not TfidfVectorizer) because LDA expects raw counts."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: BERTopic (production)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "from bertopic import BERTopic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "topic_model = BERTopic("
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    embedding_model=\"sentence-transformers/all-MiniLM-L6-v2\","
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    min_topic_size=15,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    verbose=True,"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "topics, probs = topic_model.fit_transform(documents)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "info = topic_model.get_topic_info()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "print(info.head(20))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "valid_topics = info[info[\"Topic\"] != -1][\"Topic\"].tolist()"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "for topic_id in valid_topics[:5]:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    print(f\"topic {topic_id}: {topic_model.get_topic(topic_id)[:10]}\")"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "The filter on `Topic != -1` drops BERTopic's outlier bucket (documents HDBSCAN could not cluster). `min_topic_size` controls HDBSCAN's minimum cluster size; BERTopic's library default is 10. This example sets it to 15 explicitly for the lesson's scale. For corpora over 10,000 documents, increase to 50 or 100."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: evaluation"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Both methods output topic words. The question is whether those words cohere."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Topic coherence (c_v).** Combines NPMI (normalized pointwise mutual information) of top-word pairs over sliding-window contexts, aggregates the scores into topic vectors, and compares those vectors via cosine similarity. Higher is better. Use `gensim.models.CoherenceModel` with `coherence=\"c_v\"`."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Topic diversity.** Fraction of unique words across all topics' top words. Higher is better (topics do not overlap)."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "- **Qualitative inspection.** Read the top words of each topic. Do they name a real thing? Human judgment is still the last line of defense."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Fit LDA with 5 topics on the 20 Newsgroups dataset. Print top 10 words per topic. Label each topic by hand. Did the algorithm find the real categories?\n2. **Medium.** Fit BERTopic on the same 20 Newsgroups subset. Compare the number of topics found, top words, and qualitative coherence against LDA. Which surfaces the real categories more cleanly?\n3. **Hard.** Compute c_v coherence for both LDA and BERTopic on your corpus. Run each with 5, 10, 20, 50 topics. Plot coherence vs topic count. Report which method is more stable across topic counts."
      ]
    }
  ],
